            S("Viswaroop Darsan", "Viswaroop Darsan", "Viswaroop Darsan", "ヴィシュワループ・ダルシャン"),
            S("Eighteen inches high, thirteen inches wide and eight inches deep, carved in onyx. Ramakanta began Viswaroop Darsan in 1998 and worked it for seven and a half years: the story of Vishnu held in one stone, with figures of half an inch. It is the piece named with the National Award of 2005. A letter from Dr. D. C. Ebinezar, dated 31 July 2018, records that his family acquired it.",
